    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mastering conversions between fractions, decimals, ratios, and percentages is essential for speed.",
        "Successive percentage change concepts are critical for calculating net increase or decrease across multiple stages.",
        "Reverse percentage methods are vital for finding original values prior to increases or decreases.",
        "Core application areas include Population Growth, Consumption Reduction, and Examination Score problems."
      ],
      "id": "mhyvo7o"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bfj27fa",
      "content": "The word percentage means ―per hundred.‖ It is a way of expressing a number as a fraction of 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0xt4bey",
      "content": "For example: 50% means 50 out of 100. Mathematically: 50% = 50/100 = 1/2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i0p5l8l",
      "content": "Percentages help compare quantities easily and are heavily used in arithmetic chapters such as Profit &amp; Loss, Simple Interest, Compound Interest, Ratio, and Data Interpretation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ei4b68x",
      "content": "Students must focus on understanding the meaning rather than memorizing formulas."
    },
    {
      "id": "p8az5so",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Converting Between Fractions, Decimals, and Percentages"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e1j6htl",
      "content": "Understanding conversions is essential because many problems become simpler once the correct form is used."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yyxgzxc",
      "content": "To convert a percentage into a fraction: Remove the percent sign and divide by 100. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yyvcvk6",
      "content": "25% = 25/100 = 1/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6m8whmh",
      "content": "To convert a decimal into a percentage: Multiply by 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8lgqjbs",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1yuiduk",
      "content": "0.6 × 100 = 60%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6az6efj",
      "content": "Common Values to Memorize:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w0p8acp",
      "content": "1/2 = 50%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w5znwh4",
      "content": "1/3 ≈ 33.33%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pt5a3iz",
      "content": "2/3 ≈ 66.67%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "eirc68i",
      "content": "1/4 = 25%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qgooupi",
      "content": "3/4 = 75%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "uwtcmu2",
      "content": "1/5 = 20%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "chfc6ry",
      "content": "1/8 = 12.5%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "l6nq7ts",
      "content": "1/10 = 10%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "10qn274",
      "content": "Memorizing these reduces calculation time drastically."
    },
    {
      "id": "0wyp3oq",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Basic Percentage Formula </strong>The fundamental formula is: Percentage = (Part / Whole) × 100 Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ftq79xi",
      "content": "Out of 80 students, 56 passed. Percentage = (56/80) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "rdn8abt",
      "content": "= 0.7 × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "irrt8lw",
      "content": "= 70%"
    },
    {
      "id": "smnf8oa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Finding a Percentage of a Number"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ocgqj4y",
      "content": "Formula: x% of y = (x/100) × y Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ngapa7m",
      "content": "Find 35% of 240."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w0e6v9x",
      "content": "Step 1: Convert into fraction. 35% = 35/100 = 7/20"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6yg56f3",
      "content": "Step 2: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ly0untg",
      "content": "(7/20) × 240"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sjzjx2n",
      "content": "Step 3: Simplify."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9p93bt3",
      "content": "240 ÷ 20 = 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0gu5bkt",
      "content": "Step 4: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3ui1iuq",
      "content": "12 × 7 = 84"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "rr0za23",
      "content": "Final Answer: 84"
    },
    {
      "id": "6dwy9i1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Percentage Increase"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cwnwjww",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fv011wt",
      "content": "Increase % = (Increase / Original Value) × 100 Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yq4eb8x",
      "content": "A price rises from 200 to 260."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n8umvk0",
      "content": "Increase = 60"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1bgbfnh",
      "content": "Increase % = (60/200) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4zx4b10",
      "content": "= 30%"
    },
    {
      "id": "661ek7r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Percentage Decrease"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cdq4e4r",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "46j9xex",
      "content": "Decrease % = (Decrease / Original Value) × 100 Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5ht9fbp",
      "content": "A shirt price drops from 500 to 400. Decrease = 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5hlzvkb",
      "content": "Decrease % = (100/500) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sbogg9c",
      "content": "= 20%"
    },
    {
      "id": "av45tyl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Successive Percentage Change"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "omtn4mm",
      "content": "When two percentage changes occur one after another, the second change is applied to the NEW value."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6re1xnv",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sziilix",
      "content": "Increase 10% and then increase 20%. "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "izrkdh8",
      "content": "Assume original value = 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iq5lzpw",
      "content": "After 10% increase: New value = 110"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e23auf5",
      "content": "Now find 20% of 110 = 22 Final value"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "c8bcrbu",
      "content": "=&gt;110+22=132"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ckdq55l",
      "content": "Total increase = 32"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3vbro9a",
      "content": "Net % = a + b + (ab/100)<br></br>= 10 + 20 + (10×20)/100 = <strong>32%</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z310y8s",
      "content": "<em>Important Learning: Do NOT add percentages directly.</em>"
    },
    {
      "id": "7okygc7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Successive Increase and Decrease of Same Percentage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "idnjtho",
      "content": "If a value increases by x% and then decreases by x%, the final result is always a loss. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "09z14bl",
      "content": "Increase 20% then decrease 20%. Assume original value = 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uyrlcz3",
      "content": "After increase:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "j6kbhfx",
      "content": "120"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yt3l7we",
      "content": "After decrease:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6qayn99",
      "content": "20% of 120 = 24"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "py0j5fq",
      "content": "Final value = 96 Loss = 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sh69zz1",
      "content": "Percentage loss = 4%"
    },
    {
      "id": "q8qfp97",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Reverse Percentage (Very Important for RRB)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vjs97t5",
      "content": "Used when the final value is given but the original value must be found. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ne8ftnm",
      "content": "After a 25% increase, a salary becomes 5000. Let original salary = x."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5wqcfuw",
      "content": "125% of x = 5000"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "f3s41gm",
      "content": "1.25x = 5000"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3316rkv",
      "content": "x = 5000 ÷ 1.25"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ink58e5",
      "content": "x = 4000"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pojangj",
      "content": "Verification:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kljony5",
      "content": "25% of 4000 = 1000"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zyhik4l",
      "content": "4000 + 1000 = 5000 ✔"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "82g10nh",
      "content": "Original salary = 4000"
    },
    {
      "id": "g3vvkqi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Percentage to Ratio Conversion (Step-by-Step Explanation)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0g9rfvi",
      "content": "Problem Statement:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2e6k90v",
      "content": "If A is 20% more than B, find the ratio A : B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f0gypsr",
      "content": "Step 1: Understand the meaning."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d73hoxi",
      "content": "When we say ―A is 20% more than B,‖ it means A is greater than B by 20% of B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rpv0e3a",
      "content": "Step 2: Assume a convenient value."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rp45s8a",
      "content": "Let B = 100. (Assuming 100 makes percentage calculations easier.)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t9gruf9",
      "content": "Step 3: Find 20% of B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "35yxzuv",
      "content": "20% of 100 = (20/100) × 100 = 20."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8dails2",
      "content": "Step 4: Calculate A."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "voszb1j",
      "content": "Since A is 20 more than B:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i3rkdi3",
      "content": "A = 100 + 20 = 120."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "202uuis",
      "content": "Step 5: Form the ratio."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2xfzg8m",
      "content": "A : B = 120 : 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t9nf3xp",
      "content": "Step 6: Simplify the ratio. Divide both numbers by 20."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jtmmzk7",
      "content": "120 ÷ 20 = 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lm056ni",
      "content": "100 ÷ 20 = 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vr0gkcp",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wdx9zkv",
      "content": "A : B = 6 : 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "kd741xx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Ratio to Percentage Conversion (Step-by-Step Explanation)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5u2cbzk",
      "content": "Problem Statement:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yzafl9b",
      "content": "If A : B = 5 : 4, by what percentage is A greater than B?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i9psgr4",
      "content": "Step 1: Understand the ratio."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jrz6b4u",
      "content": "The ratio tells us that when A = 5 parts, B = 4 parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "01ydv95",
      "content": "Step 2: Find the difference. Difference = 5 − 4 = 1 part."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r1u8ckf",
      "content": "Step 3: Identify the base."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w5ix0lb",
      "content": "We compare with B because the question asks how much A is greater than B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2p72bg8",
      "content": "Step 4: Convert the difference into a fraction of B. Difference/Base = 1/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1f7zo57",
      "content": "Step 5: Convert into percentage. (1/4) × 100 = 25%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "030i84o",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2q1pqm0",
      "content": "A is 25% greater than B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r2amx59",
      "content": "Important Learning:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p331c8q",
      "content": "Always divide by the base quantity when converting ratio differences into percentages."
    },
    {
      "id": "3hzh8n9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Population Growth Concept (Fully Explained)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "67i9t92",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9oatep1",
      "content": "New Population = Original × (1 + r/100)^n"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "522nsuh",
      "content": "Where:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "d7hgh4n",
      "content": "r = rate of growth"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jisyp7z",
      "content": "n = number of years"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qgflvs6",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ggn0j3t",
      "content": "Population grows by 10% every year for 2 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "grvan3p",
      "content": "Step 1: Assume original population. Let original population = 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "voankwj",
      "content": "Step 2: Apply growth for Year 1. Increase"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sxt848e",
      "content": "= 10% of 100 = 10."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e9m1mah",
      "content": "New population = 100 + 10 = 110. Step 3: Apply growth for Year 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9myjjmh",
      "content": "<em>IMPORTANT: Growth is applied to the new population, not the original.</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cr21igb",
      "content": "Increase = 10% of 110 = 11."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pdu4iiu",
      "content": "New population = 110 + 11 = 121."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f6pg8p6",
      "content": "Step 4: Find total increase. Increase = 121 − 100 = 21."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2esi0z3",
      "content": "Step 5: Convert into percentage. (21/100)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hs1ckbr",
      "content": "× 100 = 21%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rjyqinl",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nz2lzv7",
      "content": "Total population increase over 2 years is 21%, not 20%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qudb4z9",
      "content": "Key Concept:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ouffct",
      "content": "Successive growth compounds over time."
    },
    {
      "id": "owa64bf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Consumption Reduction Concept (Fully Explained)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z58zv00",
      "content": "Concept:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4ay6ymw",
      "content": "If consumption decreases, the same stock lasts longer because it is being used more slowly."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Concept",
        "Focus / Target Calculation"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Percentage to Ratio Conversion",
          "Converting percentage figures into simplified fractional ratios"
        ],
        [
          "Ratio to Percentage Conversion",
          "Expressing proportional ratios as base-100 percentage values"
        ],
        [
          "Percentage Increase",
          "Calculating enhanced values after a positive percentage shift"
        ],
        [
          "Percentage Decrease",
          "Determining reduced values after a negative percentage shift"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "ebfhulk"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "790fw8g",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4nr20lp",
      "content": "Consumption decreases by 20%. Find the increase in duration."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iftxusi",
      "content": "Step 1: Assume original consumption."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vmxm9ih",
      "content": "Let original consumption = 100 units per day."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d168uqi",
      "content": "Step 2: Apply the decrease. Decrease = 20% of 100 = 20."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pbguxbm",
      "content": "New consumption = 100 − 20 = 80 units."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4iitx66",
      "content": "Step 3: Understand the relationship."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xdbp3st",
      "content": "Duration is inversely proportional to consumption."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l3x9vh0",
      "content": "If consumption becomes smaller, duration becomes larger."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mv4tyvm",
      "content": "Step 4: Calculate the increase in duration."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6am49mv",
      "content": "New duration / Old duration = Old consumption / New consumption"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "cgugnq9",
      "content": "= 100 / 80"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2voxg13",
      "content": "= 1.25"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wsenkb7",
      "content": "Step 5: Convert to percentage. Increase = 1.25 − 1 = 0.25"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lhuc86j",
      "content": "0.25 × 100 = 25%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gi4r9hh",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hhntwpr",
      "content": "The stock will last 25% longer."
    },
    {
      "id": "dq1xura",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Examination Score Problem (Fully Explained)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uuyjoci",
      "content": "Problem:A student scores 30% and fails by 12 marks. Another student scores 40% and passes by 8 marks. Find the total marks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2mcefqy",
      "content": "Step 1: Understand the gap."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t6fqnq9",
      "content": "The difference between failing and passing marks is: 12 + 8 = 20 marks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5yjisnq",
      "content": "Step 2: Find percentage difference. 40% − 30% = 10%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pz5hm19",
      "content": "Step 3: Interpret."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nott1r4",
      "content": "10% of total marks equals 20 marks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cetil3h",
      "content": "Step 4: Calculate total marks. Let total marks = x."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "eqd9ko5",
      "content": "10% of x = 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k9wi8u2",
      "content": "(10/100)x = 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qwz9ua6",
      "content": "0.1x = 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yacigbe",
      "content": "x = 20 ÷ 0.1"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "maja94f",
      "content": "x = 200"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1l9pzqw",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c61l1xy",
      "content": "Total marks = 200."
    },
    {
      "id": "daokpfs",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Solved Examples (Fully Explained) Example 1: Find 125% of 64."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "znyn723",
      "content": "Step 1: Convert percentage into fraction. 125% = 125/100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e4ab4rn",
      "content": "Step 2: Simplify. 125/100 = 5/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kp5vfn6",
      "content": "Step 3: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ptvh2of",
      "content": "(5/4) × 64"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "209agdv",
      "content": "Step 4: Simplify before multiplying. 64"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sftvuoa",
      "content": "÷ 4 = 16"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "50wxmnq",
      "content": "Step 5: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "epy8y1t",
      "content": "16 × 5 = 80"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k3ff0da",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "24q6qj6",
      "content": "125% of 64 is 80."
    },
    {
      "id": "rb5pd3e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 2: A number is decreased by 30% and becomes 140. Find the original number."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nv73zpo",
      "content": "Step 1: Understand the meaning."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lp42d3j",
      "content": "If decreased by 30%, then 70% remains."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dxytswz",
      "content": "Step 2: Let original number = x. 70% of x = 140"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kg6l6if",
      "content": "(70/100)x = 140"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6i77wqq",
      "content": "0.7x = 140"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p52ckjb",
      "content": "Step 3: Solve."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ryx2pn7",
      "content": "x = 140 ÷ 0.7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "atv8iws",
      "content": "x = 200"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ox9lem3",
      "content": "Step 4: Verification."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "imd2kza",
      "content": "30% of 200 = 60"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pecofp0",
      "content": "200 − 60 = 140 ✔"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bww97hb",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "biylp6i",
      "content": "Original number = 200."
    },
    {
      "id": "169sstr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 3: Find the net change when a salary increases by 10% and then 20%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "62j4x8k",
      "content": "Step 1: Assume original salary = 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r7996n6",
      "content": "Step 2: First increase. 10% of 100 = 10"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Reverse Percentage is explicitly designated as a high-frequency topic for RRB examinations.",
        "Successive percentage changes (e.g., salary increasing by 10% and then 20%) are frequently tested in competitive aptitude tests.",
        "Consumption Reduction and Population Growth problems require quick back-and-forth conversion between ratios and percentages."
      ],
      "id": "8wpvici"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "048ohq2",
      "content": "New salary = 110."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "btq4uf7",
      "content": "Step 3: Second increase. 20% of 110 = 22"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5vgq799",
      "content": "New salary = 132."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2g0b4nz",
      "content": "Step 4: Find total increase."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "afac99p",
      "content": "132 − 100 = 32."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5xxal6f",
      "content": "Step 5: Convert into percentage. (32/100)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "klyq524",
      "content": "× 100 = 32%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "plm6d3j",
      "content": "<em>Important Note:Percentages cannot be added directly because the second increase applies to the updated value.</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6q6s80g",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b9bimid",
      "content": "Net increase = 32%."
    },
    {
      "id": "nq33t6d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Practice Questions with VERY DETAILED Solutions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nzpul2p",
      "content": "Question 1:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lnavne7",
      "content": "Find 45% of 360. Solution:"
